Hmm.. - I already told you about my nuclide chart from 1974. WRT Astatine
I cannot quite see what you mean. Astatin is a product of two of the major
natural decay chains, Actinium (U235->...->At219 resp. At215->...) and
Uran (U238->...->At218->...), which is also confirmed by above wiki link.
At least one isotope of every element below U is part of the natural decay
chains, so I'd answer your question as "There are 92 elements that are
natural elements or products thereof." OTOH, above Bi(83) there are only
four isotopes marked as primordial, Th232, U234, U235, and U238. Whether
Po, At, Rn, Fr, Ra, Ac, Pa shall be considered natural I can't say.

